ged. VALIDATION with the same model and settings: (1) Cu lattice constant 3.626 A vs experiment about 3.615 A (+0.3%), passes. (2) Isolated-atom-referenced quantities fail. The Cu cohesive energy is 3.16 eV vs experiment 3.49 eV (Kittel, Introduction to Solid State Physics), so it is underbound by 0.33 eV. The O2 binding energy is 5.53 eV vs experiment De about 5.21 eV (D0 = 5.12 eV, Huber & Herzberg) and vs PBE about 6.0-6.2 eV, so the model matches neither. (3) A literature PBE value from a web search (arXiv:2505.12914, VASP-PBE, isolated gas-phase O reference) gives fcc -5.00 / hcp -4.91 eV; I could not confirm that paper's coverage. MACE is about 0.56 eV weaker than this, and its fcc > hcp ordering agrees. ALTERNATIVE (well-posed) estimate: model E_ads vs 1/2 O2 (-1.67 eV) minus half the experimental O2 De (2.61 eV) gives -4.28 eV. UNCERTAINTY +/-0.6 eV covers the spread across the MACE value, this alternative and the PBE literature value, plus the isolated-atom reference error (0.3-0.6 eV). Finite size and slab thickness contribute <0.01 eV; the fcc/hcp ordering contributes 0.014 eV. Not included: the spread across DFT functionals (PBE is known to overbind O on metals; RPBE is weaker by several tenths of an eV), zero-point energy (about 0.05-0.07 eV), thermal effects and coverage beyond 0.25 ML. No experimental atom-referenced value was used or claimed.\"\n}\nEOF\n./board post property_result @/work/scripts/result.json --parent e2d05567-74c1-4863-95ad-81dab0497e6b"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2141,"cache_read_input_tokens":41225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2141,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d73de39-d716-4340-ab